# sprint-169 / Sprint 1 — minimise build context while preserving every input
# the Rust crate, the Vite/Tauri build, and the E2E specs read.
#
# Every exclusion added here MUST be checked against those three readers first.
# In particular:
#   - tests/fixtures/** is REQUIRED whenever the crate's tests compile —
#     src-tauri/table-view-core/src/db/postgres/schema.rs (inside `#[cfg(test)]`) and
#     src-tauri/tests/fixture_loading.rs both
#     include_str! tests/fixtures/fk_reference_samples.json.
#   - e2e/**/*.spec.ts is REQUIRED at runtime — keep the e2e/ tree included
#     except for the host-only report dir.

# ---- Generated / cache artefacts (regenerated inside the image) ----
node_modules
src-tauri/target
# #1769 — `table-view-core` builds standalone into its own target dir, which
# `src-tauri/target` above does not cover.
src-tauri/table-view-core/target
target
dist
coverage
*.tsbuildinfo

# ---- Version control / CI metadata (not read by the build) ----
.git
.gitignore
.github

# ---- Editor / OS junk ----
.vscode
.idea
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# ---- Local-only secrets (never bake into image) ----
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ---- Documentation / memory palace (no Cargo `readme = ...`,
#      no include_str! callsite references *.md or docs/ — audited) ----
*.md
docs/
memory/
.claude

# ---- Host-only test reporter output ----
e2e/wdio-report
wdio-report
test-results
tmp
